+    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
 **What it does**
 
-Segemehl_ is a short read mapper with gaps.
+Segemehl is a short read mapper with gaps.
+
+Segemehl maps short sequencer reads to reference genomes. Unlike other methods, segemehl
+is able to detect not only mismatches but also insertions and deletions. Furthermore,
+segemehl is not limited to a specific read length and is able to map primer- or
+polyadenylation contaminated reads correctly. segemehl implements a matching strategy
+based on enhanced suffix arrays (ESA) and supports bisulfite sequencing mapping and split
+read mapping.
+
+-----
+
+**Inputs**
+
+Reads can be given as FASTQ or FASTA, plain or gzip-compressed. Paired-end libraries are
+supplied as one first-strand and one second-strand file. The reference genome is either
+taken from the history (uncompressed FASTA, the index is then built on the fly) or from a
+pre-built segemehl index installed by your Galaxy administrator.
 
-Segemehl_ is a software to map short sequencer reads to reference genomes.
-Unlike other methods, segemehl is able to detect not only mismatches but also insertions and deletions.
-Furthermore, segemehl is not limited to a specific read length and is able to mapprimer- or polyadenylation contaminated reads correctly.
-segemehl implements a matching strategy based on enhanced suffix arrays (ESA). Segemehl_ allows bisulfite sequencing mapping and split read mapping.
+-----
 
-.. _Segemehl: http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/Software/segemehl/
+**Outputs**
 
+The main output is a SAM alignment file. Optionally the unmapped reads can be written to a
+separate FASTQ file.
 
